1 NOTE {geni:about_me} ==Karin Tordsdotter Store==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Tord Björnsson Store and Kerstin Bengtsdotter Krabbe 
2 CONT
2 CONT *  Björnsson Store , about 1508. To Torestorp and Högalid in Ambjörnarps parish, Älvsborg County. Called the well-born sven 1473-01-02, when he loved the warden Björn Bengtsson to Hällekis [half-animal] about his grandfather's pro
2 CONC perty, Trollåsa 1, as "his parents have been charged for many years". Mentioned in several letters from the 1480s and 1490s 1 . Seen primarily in the committee at Kinds of the City 3 1491-05-14. He brought [the sparrow without sta
2 CONC r] in the shield on Snake 2 and can not be merged with his contemporary name Tord Björnsson in Bragnem (1487-1516), who in the gun brought two sparrows without star. They sealed each other's letters and were probably liberated. Ma
2 CONC rried to Christina Crab by Svaneby . Daughter of Bengt Crab to Kärra in Halland County and Gunnild Gunnarsdotter Gylta.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Married==
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: '''Peder Hard of Segerstad,''' son of Olof Pedersson,). Squire. Mentioned as early as 1501, when after his father he joined as a party to a criminal case concerning the estate Landbotorp in Håksvik's parish. Brought two
2 CONC  crossbeams as a shield. Died in Stockholm about 1534 (after 1532-06-24). Married to Carin Tordsdotter , daughter of the captain Tord Björnsson ( Store ) and Kerstin Bengtsdotter Krabbe .
2 CONT
2 CONT ==Children==
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Lars Pedersson,''' to Segerstad and Svanseryd in Torestorp parish Älvsborg County, Hjällö in Fågelås parish Skaraborg County and Bolmstad in Angelstad parish Kronoberg County, which he replaced by King Gustaf 1559 41 . Comman
2 CONC der in Vartofta and others. the district 1536-01-31-1540 at Höjentorp's royal estate in Eggby parish Skaraborgs county 1540-06-18. Deliveries from there are still in 1543. The governor of Västbo hardened in 1541-1543 14 . Joined i
2 CONC n Hovs county in 1542. Provisioned as on 2/10. Sealed Västerås Heritage Association 1544-01-13. Received pp. 6/7 in the training Villstads parish and 1547-05-04 Långaryds parish in Västbo hardened. County Governor in Sunnerbo s. O
2 CONC n 1 4. Fogde at Stegeborg 1547-05-13-1554. Received 1551-01-09 in extension Häradshammar parish in Östkind's hardened Östergötland county in consideration for the aforementioned parishes. Also lost Häradshammar in 1554, but had th
2 CONC e interest of church, priest and prebend villagers in Västbo hardened to his death. Governor in Kinnevald 1558 and 1559 15 . Konf.fullm. at Sunnerbo district court 2 pp. on 15/12. Sealed cone. Gustaf I's will 1560-06-30 the grant 
2 CONC of the states 1561-04-15. Commander of the Army in 1560. Jämte Jakob Bagge served as Admiral of the Navy in Älvsborg 16 1561-10-04. Hövidsman at Älvsborg page 17/10 during Sigvard Kruse's illness 17 . Colonel for the artillery in 
2 CONC 1562 and for the war people in Västergötland 181563-04-28. Stupade s. Å. In nov. at Halmstad [Al]. Married 1552-09-25 with Brita Ribbing , born 1530 at Svanseryd, died 12 1592 (after 19/2), daughter of governor Nils Knutsson Ribbi
2 CONC ng Anna Olofsdotter ( Stenbock ).
2 CONT * '''Krabbe''''Pedersson,''' died 1566. Married to Sigrid Hansdotter.
2 CONT *''' Brita,''' died before 1573, married 1st with the bailiff in Allbo Östbo cures Arvid Olofsson Drake, ( Drake from Västbo ). Married 2nd: with the commander at Kronoberg Göran Jönsson ( Swan ).
2 CONT * ''' Ingrid,''' married to Clemet Månsson Stolpe .
2 CONT * '''Anna,''' married to Velam German.
2 CONT *''' Gunnil,''' married before 1532-06-24 with his sister-in-law Claes Olofsson Drake ( Drake from Västbo ).
2 CONT *''' Carin,''' married to Matts Torbjörnsson.
2 CONT * '''Magdalena,''' dead unmarried in the 1590s.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' Adliga family Hard of Segerstad No. 17, Tab 5 - https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/H%C3%A5rd_af_Segerstad_nr_17
2 CONT
