1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Erik Gudmundsson (son of Gudmund Pedersson, table 1), to Låstad in Furingstad parish, Östergötland county and Vrangsjö in Marbäck parish, Jönköping county. Equestrian during King Erik's time. Was present at the mus
2 CONC ter with the savior in Östergötland in 15626. Died in 1564 at Vrangsjö as a result of a gunshot wound, which he received in the battle at Ronneby, and buried in Marbäck's church. Married in 1555 to Ingeborg Marbo in her 1st marria
2 CONC ge (married 2nd to bailiff Jöns Eriksson [Rosenstråle no. 37|Rosenstråle] in his 2nd marriage)10, daughter of the castle bailiff at Stegeborg, chamber councilor Truls Andersson. Printer (Marbo), to Ravanäs, who in the coat of arms
2 CONC  carried half a lily and a star, and his 3rd wife Karin Eriksdotter Slatte. Child: Card (Wolf). Court lieutenant 1586. Lieutenant at Östgöta cavalry 1590. Participated in the said year's campaign to Ivangorod and Novgorod and had 
2 CONC to be left behind in Viborg during the return march to Finland due to illness. Died there 1591-02-28. Married to Kerstin N. N., who survived. [12] Gustaf Eriksson Ulf. Second lieutenant. Died 1601. See Tab. 6 Kerstin Eriksdotter U
2 CONC lf, to Låstad, which she probably inherited from her grandmother. Lived in 1620. Married 1692-01-0024 to13 war commissioner and secretary Henrik Mattsson Huggut, knighted by King Johan III 1583-01-08, in his 3rd marriage (married 
2 CONC 1st to Karin Nilsdotter, sister of Anders Nilsson to Tali [ Sabelfana], ennobled 16/06/1583 to Cecilia Johansdotter, died 1590/05/05 Bjurböle Eriksson Ulf, born 1564. See Tab 7
