1 NOTE {geni:about_me} https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82#TAB_2
2 CONT
2 CONT = Arvid Jönsson Drake af Intorp=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Jöns Bengtsson and Birgitta Erlandsdotter Bååt 
2 CONT * Old Salvation Family, introduced 1625. † 1635. (Also referred to as [Sparrow over star] or (Sparrow from Intorp))
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1376 in Gällstad, Ulricehamn, Västra Götaland County, Sweden
2 CONT * Death:	December 14, 1438 (57-66) in Barne Åsaka, Barne, Essunga, Västra Götaland County, Sweden
2 CONT * [https://www.findagrave.com/memorial/161184011/arvid-j_nsson-drake_af_intorp '''Arvid Jönsson Drake af Intorp Find A Grave Memorial''']
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82 Noble Family Drake af Intorp nr 82, by Adelsvapen]
2 CONT
2 CONT Arvid Jönsson (son of Jöns Bengtsson, Tab. 1 ), born around 1376, latest 1438. District chief. Squire. He still carried 1412-05-26 the same weapon as his father (chevron), but 1421-05-03 and later chevron over a star. '''Married b
2 CONC efore 1416 to Ingegärd Petersdotter , died no later than 1438, daughter of the gunsmith Peter Andersson (Prika) and Ingeborg Sigvidsdotter (Ribbing).
2 CONT '''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Knut Arvidsson.''' District Chief. Died 1459. to Torpa in Länghem parish, Älvsborg county. Called a gunsmith 1438-12-14. District chief in Kinds district still 1458. Died 1459 (RHKn.). '''Married 1439 to Kerstin Bengtsdotter 
2 CONC (Kompan) , widow lived 1459, daughter of the Halland gunsmith Bengt Turesson ( Kompan , chevron over leaves) and Märta Gunnarsdotter (Gylta).'''
2 CONT * '''Arvid Arvidsson Squire''' Made farm change (RHKn.) With his brother Knut Arvidsson 1457-09-25. Lived 1490. '''Married 1477-07-14 (morning gift) at Högnalöv in Uråsa parish, Kronoberg county, when he gave a mill in Intorp and 
2 CONC a farm in Risatorp, both in Gällstad parish, Älvsborg county and Långhult in Burseryd parish, Jönköping county in morning gift (RHKn.), with Ingegärd Gregersdotter, daughter of Gregers Svensson ( in Värend) and NN Nilsdotter (Balk
2 CONC  by Billa)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT http://daten.digitale-sammlungen.de/~db/bsb00000600/images/index.html?seite=968&fip=193.174.98.30
2 CONT
2 CONT Pedersdotters, (Bielke) skiktbols f.47, RHA; incorrectly different according to the colorless image caption in SoH 1955, p. 195) or yellow and blue (Gen42, b. 34) or white and blue (Raneke, 3:87). Remains of the family's archive c
2 CONC an be found in the Kantzowska archive (E 4340-4341) in RA (some letters printed in VFT I: 8-9, p.96-114) with provenance from Ingierd Gylta's (tab.6) granddaughter's husband Gustaf Soop's descendants on Hjulsta in Enköpings-Näs. O
2 CONC ther remains have come to UUB from the manuscript collector Professor Oscar Quensel (cf. B. Broomé, The Manuscript Collectors and the Swedish Archives, 1977, p.398). Some 15th century letters for members of the Gylta family are kn
2 CONC own through transcripts in the sparse copybook B 16 in RA. Farmers with the names Anders Gylta, Erik Gylta, Lars Gylta and Måns Gylta are mentioned in Mark's hd's judgment books during the first decades of the 17th century (remark
2 CONC  by engineer RolfEkelund, Kullavik). It is uncertain whether Gylta in their case is a nickname, or whether it is due to kinship with the savior family Gylta. Literature. C. G. St) 'ffe, Om slägten Gylta (\ rFT I; 8-9, 1897, s. 97 
2 CONC f.); K. H. Karlsson, Vadstenanunnan Ingegärd Persdotter's (Gylta) letter to her nephew Bengt Gylta with an account of the Gylta family's family connections (PHT 1907, pp. 67-72); K. K: son Leijonhufrud, Minor contributions to the 
2 CONC Gylta family's personal history (PHT 1909, p. 23 ff.); J. E. Almquist, The Oral Tradition and the Noble Family Gylta (SoH 1955, p. 18F201); H. Gillingstam, Gylta (SBL 17,1967-69, p.635 ff.). 
