3 CITY Höreda (F)
3 CTRY Sweden
1 OCCU
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Anna Pedersdotter Svenske=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Daughter of Häradshövding (District Chief) Petrus Petri Svenske and Catharina Larsdotter Bröms
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Svenske_nr_258 Noble family Swedish no. 258]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Petrus Petri Svenske (son of Peder Svenske,''' Tab. 1. ), born circa 1525. Died 1591. Ordained priest 1559. Pastor of the Höreda and Mellby parishes of the Diocese of Linköping 1560. '''Married 1570 to Catharina Bröms , daughte
2 CONC r of the chieftain Lars Bröms , no. 161, and Margareta Drake, of the old Drake family. The couple had four sons in addition to their daughters.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Children''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Abel.''' Drowned in 1612 at Vittsjö.
2 CONT * '''Margareta'''. Married 1st to Erik Persson (half-deer), executed for murder. Married 2nd to Axel Axelsson.
2 CONT * '''Elin'''. Married to the goldsmith and councilor of Mariestad Sven Månsson (grandfather of Sven Hasselbom, ennobled Hasselbom, no. 1332 ).
2 CONT * '''Anna'''. Married to the councilor of Brätte Börje Olofsson. (ancestor of the noble families Tigerhielm no. 817 and Karlström no. 963 ).
2 CONT * '''Beata''', born 1585, died 1645-04-14. Married in 1603 to the vicar of Höreda Petrus Nicolai Skarp. (father of Lieutenant Colonel Isak Skarp, ennobled Skarpenfelt, later Skarp von Felt no. 517. )
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.cronbergsgenealogi.se/wp/?p=89 Did Anna Persdotter Svenske exist?]
2 CONT
2 CONT Through the Carlberg and Carlström families, including the noble families Tigerhielm and Karlström, Anna Persdotter Svenske can be found on many Swedish family trees. Her father is said to have been the vicar Petrus Petri Svenske 
2 CONC († 1591) in Höreda, Småland, and through her mother Karin Larsdotter Bröms, one quickly returns to medieval Salvation families and, by extension, through Canute the Holy's wife Adele, to Charlemagne in France. In the early 1980s, 
2 CONC I researched her roots according to the literature available at the time, from articles in Personhistorisk tidskrift and Släkt och hävd.
2 CONT
2 CONT The Anna Persdotter in question was married to the alderman of Brätte Börje Olofsson. Ulf Barck-Holst has written the book Brätte stad och dombok. Brätte was located on Lake Vänern and was a predecessor to Vänersborg. However, Vän
2 CONC ersborg burned down in 1834 and with it old archival documents were destroyed. However, there is a dombok preserved from 1615 and a few tax lists. Börje Olofsson is mentioned in the 1610 tax list as the highest taxed person in Brä
2 CONC tte, but he does not appear in the dombok and had probably died before 1615. Barck-Holst also states that Börje Olofsson would have had twelve children, but I have not found this information in Anrep's Swedish nobility genealogy t
2 CONC ables, to which he refers.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''The inheritance dispute between Lars Bröms and Margareta Drake'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In 2002, however, the chairman of the Genealogical Society, Ian Hamilton, published an article “Priests may well eat pancakes and lamb shanks” – About the family circle of the vicar Peder Skarps and his wife Beata Svenske (Släkt o
2 CONC ch Hävd 2002:2, pp. 104-135) about an inheritance dispute in which Beata Svenske and her husband are trying to get a share of the inheritance of her grandparents. This inheritance had gone to the daughters who married into the nob
2 CONC ility and not to the daughters who married commoners. Hamilton notes that neither Anna Persdotter Svenske nor her sister Elin, who was married to the councilman and goldsmith in Mariestad, Sven Månsson, are mentioned in the case, 
2 CONC even if they or their children had the same interest. That made me put a parenthesis about Anna's ancestors for the time being, and thought that some explanation would probably emerge in the future.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Son Anders Börjesson'''
2 CONT
2 CONT My interest in Anna Persdotter Svenske's lineage was rekindled when last year I received an inquiry about a possible son Anders Börjesson who appears on a family tree. The cavalry master Elias Mallien of the Southern Scanian Caval
2 CONC ry Regiment is said to have been married twice. The last time to Katarina Caroch, but also once before to an Anna Andersdotter, who was said to be the daughter of a county clerk Anders Börjesson, who in turn was said to be the son
2 CONC  of Börje Olofsson and Anna Persdotter Svenske. However, I have not been able to substantiate this derivation.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''What does the genealogical literature say?'''
2 CONT
2 CONT All literature is actually consistent and states that Börje Olofsson's wife was Anna Persdotter Svenske. For example, this is stated in Anrep's Svenska Adelns ättartavlor and in Elgenstierna's Den introdurade svenska adelns ättart
2 CONC avlor. If you try to go back in time, you will also find this information in the latter half of the 18th century in Abraham Hülpher's genealogical collections and in Fredrik Fryxell's Wärmelands Slägte-Bok. The information thus ha
2 CONC s old origins. Hülpher's refers to Fryxell, so Fryxell is probably the oldest source. Fredrik Fryxell (1724-1805) wrote Wärmlands Slägte-Bok. I do not know if it is dated or if he wrote on it his whole life. But it can be stated t
2 CONC hat the earliest that the tradition is recorded is in the 1750s, as I have found.
2 CONT
2 CONT {{https://www.geni.com/media/proxy?media_id= 6000000214758034832&size=large}}
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Funeral sermon after Johan Börjesson (Carlberg)'''
2 CONT
2 CONT In connection with the death of his son Johan Börjesson (Carlberg) in 1676, there is a printed funeral sermon that also contains personal details at the end, i.e. a biography of his life. As it happens, there is a copy of this fun
2 CONC eral sermon at Växjö City Library, which is why I naturally ordered it and photographed it.
2 CONT
2 CONT In this the following is written about his parents: “ The father was an honorable and well-loved Börge Oloffsson, a noble merchant and resident of Gamble Brätte Stadh: The mother was an honorable and virtuous matron, wife Anna Ped
2 CONC ers=Daughter, both of whom have fallen asleep in the Lord .”
2 CONT
2 CONT Furthermore: — “God gave him through thes Sal. Sister honorable and virtuous matron wife Britta Börges Daughter, then blessing that she through her mediation and promotion then Wälborne and Sal. Frw Anna at Granstorp for her k Bro
2 CONC ther to Caution and Bond was able” …
2 CONT
2 CONT Johan Börjesson's parents are called nobles and not well-born, which is correct since they were not nobles. Even though Anna Pedersdotter belonged to the Svenske family, she should still not be called well-born because her father 
2 CONC Petrus Svenske was a priest and thus belonged to the clergy and not the nobility even though he was of noble descent. At the same time, it was often the case that people were happy to highlight a noble lineage even if it was a cou
2 CONC ple of generations back. I think it is strange that it does not say "of the old Svenske family" or something similar about Anna Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have not been able to locate Johan's sister Britta Börjesdotter, who was probably older than him, since she helped him in the beginning. I have also not been able to figure out who Mrs. Anna at Granstorp is. She is called well-b
2 CONC orn and should therefore be a noblewoman. There is a Granstorp in Fryele sn in Småland, but it does not seem to have been a manor in the 17th century but only in the 18th century.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Factors that speak against'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Most importantly, I have not yet found any solid evidence that Anna Persdotter belonged to the Svenske family. I think it should have been mentioned in the funeral sermon for her son. Her sons Johan or Gustav Börjesson could also 
2 CONC have been parties to the case that their possible aunt Beata Svenske was pursuing together with her husband about the inheritance of their grandmother.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Factors that speak in favor'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The tradition of Anna Persdotter Svenske goes back to 18th century genealogists. Fredrik Fryxell was a chamberlain at the Trollhätte lock construction and may have had access to documents from Brätte or Vänersborg that went up in 
2 CONC smoke in connection with the city fire in 1834.
2 CONT
2 CONT Hans Kihlström has posted a notice on the Anbytarforum about an indication of a relationship between the Börjessons and Svenske. In a letter from Gustaf Börjesson to the cornet Gustaf Pålman, who was married to Anders Lennartsson 
2 CONC Svenske's daughter Christina Svenske, that for the sake of good friendship and kinship he waives a debt that Pålman had on his father-in-law's side to Börjesson. Hans Kihlström finds no other relationship but believes that it woul
2 CONC d be a relationship through Anna Persdotter. Gustaf Pålman would then be the husband of Gustaf Börjesson's cousin's granddaughter.
2 CONT
2 CONT I have had difficulty understanding why a priest in the Eksjö area in Småland would have any contact with Brätte, but Kerstin Bjernevik has drawn my attention to the fact that Anna Persdotter Svenske's cousin, the district governo
2 CONC r Peder Svenske in Väne district, was resident at Rånnum in Västra Tunhems sn at the end of the 16th century. Rånnum is located a couple of km outside Vänersborg on the east side of the Göta River. Thus, there is a reasonable geog
2 CONC raphical connection.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Could DNA verify kinship?'''
2 CONT
2 CONT The only possibility to verify a relationship between mother and daughter in the 17th century would be if one could show that descendants on a certain direct female line have the same mitochondrial DNA as direct female descendants
2 CONC  on the family line one wants to verify. Here, one encounters difficulties already when it comes to Anna Persdotter's children, since only two sons Johan and Gustaf Börjesson are known. It is therefore not a feasible path as long 
2 CONC as one does not find descendants on a direct female line.
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Another mystery'''
2 CONT
2 CONT According to Carlquist's Lund diocese herdaminne, the aforementioned cavalry chief Elias Mallien († 1709) was married to an Anna Andersdotter, who was the daughter of the county sheriff Anders Börjesson. He was in turn reportedly 
2 CONC the son of Börje Olofsson and Anna Persdotter. I have not been able to find out what source of origin is the basis for this information. For Elias Mallien's children, I have only found a couple of birth records, but they do not st
2 CONC ate the mother's name. I also lack information about when Elias married his second wife Catharina Caroch. If the information about Anna Andersdotter and her lineage is correct, one can wonder which source may have given rise to th
2 CONC is information. What I can think of is an inheritance dispute or estate inventory of some childless sibling of Anders Börjesson that took place after Anders himself had died, so that his children and their relatives are listed. Is
2 CONC  it possible to find such a document?
2 CONT
2 CONT =Further research=
2 CONT
2 CONT In a way, it may feel like a needle in a haystack, but it would be exciting if additional clues could be found. Possible search paths could be:
2 CONT
2 CONT * Is it possible to find an estate inventory for a Börjesson or Börjesdotter that lists nephews and nieces?
2 CONT * Is it possible to locate daughter Britta Börjesdotter or Johan Börjesson's benefactor, the well-born wife Anna at Granstorp?
2 CONT * Is there any crucial information in connection with Anna Persdotter's sister Elin, who was married to the goldsmith in Mariestad, Sven Månsson, who was the ancestor of the noble family Hasselbom?
2 CONT * Is there any important information at Riddarhuset?
2 CONT * Is there any information in the Palmskiöld collection?
2 CONT * If anyone has any important pieces of the puzzle, please let me know. It would be interesting to see if it is possible to verify that Anna Persdotter is of Swedish descent or not.
