1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Håkan Fadersson Thun, till Attorp and Ericstada =
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Karl Tun
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003897399632?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000137022035893 '''Ingrid Knutsdotter Drake af Intorp,'''] daughter of Knut Arvidsson, till Torpa (Sparre över Stjärna) and Kerst
2 CONC in Bengtsdotter (Kompan).  Håkan Pedersson, to Flagelsrnm and Dansjö and  and Tranetorp in Westergötbland; Was 1530 and 1550 Stath8llare in Westergöthland and carried a white hand in a blue field. - Married to Christina Thun; daug
2 CONC hter of Hakan Fadersson Thun, of Attorp and Ericsstada, who carried in the coat of arms a growing crescent moon with face and two stars facing each other against the face, and Ingegerd Knutsdotter (Drake af Intorp or Store). 
2 CONT
2 CONT Ingrid Knutsdotter. (kallas även Ingegärd) Gift med väpnaren Håkan Karlsson Tun.
2 CONT https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Drake_af_Intorp_nr_82
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Knut Hakanson''' died childless in 1518, district judge
2 CONT * '''Sigrid Håkansdotter Tun,''' died childless, married to Anders Bengtsson from Fly in Husaby parish.
2 CONT * '''Christina Håkansdotter Tun,''' married to Håkan Persson (Hand) and had Issue.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sv.m.wikipedia.org/wiki/Thun_(%C3%A4tt) Thun a Swedish and Finnish Noble Family, by Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT Thun was a Swedish and Finnish noble family who, among other farms, owned Attorp in Herrljunga municipality , Västra Götaland county . The family is believed to have become extinct before Sweden's Knights' House was founded in 162
2 CONC 5, which is why it was never introduced there as a nobility.
2 CONT
2 CONT Weapons: According to Gabriel Anrep , the family carries a growing crescent moon with a face and two stars on top of each other against the face 
2 CONT
2 CONT Håkan Fadersson Thun, to Attorp and Ericsstada , married to Ingegerd Knutsdotter ( Drake af Intorp or Store ). 
2 CONT Christina Håkansdotter (Thun) was married to Håkan Pedersson ( Hand ). 
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Oxehufvud_nr_102 Oxehufvud nr 102 Introd. 1625, by Nobility Wikipedia]
2 CONT
2 CONT '''TAB 2'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Jöns Bosson , (son of Bo Andersson, Tab. 1), to Älmestad in Hållstad parish, Älvsborg county. Fogde i Vartofta härad dels 1555-03-23–1559, dels 1562–1563 3 . Witnessed among the nobility King Gustaf I's will 1560-06-30 and partici
2 CONC pated in the estate grant 1561-04-15. Bailiff at Jönköping and in Habo parish 1563–1564 5 . Sentenced to death 1564-01-06 by King Erik's tribunal, but pardoned 5 . Castle bailiff at Varberg 1566-09-25. Lived still 1568. 6. Married
2 CONC  around 1540 to Brita Håkansdotterdotter by Håkan Pedersson ( Hand ) and his 1st wife Christina Håkansdotter (Thun).
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Märta Jönsdotter,''' died in childbirth 1569-04-25. Married 1568-06-27 in Älmestad to the Riksrådet and the governor Peder Svensson Ribbing in his 1st marriage, born 1544, died 1604.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT
