1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Beata Persdotter Gyllensvärd (nr.240)=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002322154651&photo_id=6000000168182462066&position=0 '''Daughter of Per Joensson Gyllensvärd and Elisabet Håkansdotter (Hand)''']
2 CONT * Birth:	circa 1621 in Önnarp.Hossna, Åsundenleden, Sweden
2 CONT * Dingelvik; In 1664 it was Jöns Svinhufvud's homestead: in 1681 by Mrs. Beata Gyllenswaard, Bågenholm is then referred to as the old homestead. Made until 1790 by the contract priest, Doctor Anders Sörström in Hesselskog: 1795 by
2 CONC  his widow in 1809 by Carl Fr. Owl;
2 CONT * Through acquisition, Peder and Elisabeth formed the manors of Önnarp in Skåne and Hössna in Västergötland Sweden.
2 CONT *'''Donations in Västervik, Femsjö and tax exemption in Önnarp'''. - In a letter from 7 October 1620 it appears that Per Jonsson had been promoted to lieutenant and that he received a farm in Västervik as a donation. In 1624 he re
2 CONC ceived the Yaböke estate and the Gullnubb croft in Femsjö parish as a donation (the Yaböke estate would later be taken over by his granddaughter Maria Catharina Svinhufvud and Johan Carl Rosenschantz). Per had risen further in the
2 CONC  ranks, now he was a captain. On 3 March 1629 he received in a letter from Gustav II Adolf, tax exemption on a tax home in Önnarp, as well as on his own tax farm in Hössna in Västergötland, as well as on four crofts, Hallen, Hästh
2 CONC agen and Höghult in Hössna and Tuskan in Liared parish in Redvägs district in Västergötland. According to one source, Per had purchased Hössna a few years earlier. Another source claims that it came through the marriage to Elisabe
2 CONC th, which I think is most likely. Per was now promoted to Ryttmästare. 
2 CONT * Death:	November 11, 1698 in Laxarby, i Steneby (P), Sweden
2 CONT
2 CONT =Married=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Married: [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000002322154651&photo_id=6000000168182462066&position=1 '''Jons Carlsson-Svinhuvud (af Västergötland)'''] on December 13, 1646 in Asundenleden Sweden. Son 
2 CONC of Major Carl Jönsson Svinhufvud of Västergötland and Margareta Lennartsdotter Svenske.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT *  '''Elizabeth Jonsdotter Svinhufvud,''' born in 1647 in Röksberg, Mulseryd förs, Jönköpings län (F), Sverige (Sweden)
2 CONT * '''Johan Magnus Jönsson-Svinhuvud (af Västergötland),''' born on 11 April 1649 in Röksberg, Mulseryd förs, Jönköpings län (F), Sverige (Sweden) & died on 1682 i Mulseryd (F) Sweden.
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396711&photo_id=6000000089040702855&position=1 '''Maria Catharina Jonsdotter Svinhufvud''']  born on 13 March 1650 in  i Röksberg, Mulseryd (F). died on 17
2 CONC 20-02-11 i Lilla Duvhult, Femsjö (N). Burial was on 1720-02-28 i Femsjö (N). 
2 CONT * '''Carl Jönsson Svinhufvud'''
2 CONT * '''Grace Jonsdotter Svinhufvud,''' born after June 17,1659 is apparent from the letter she sent to Per Brahe on 29 June, where Beata tells him her husband Jons has died on June 17, 1659 and she has given birth to a small daughte
2 CONC r and wishes Per Brahe to be her Godfather. Grace was baptized on July 3 1659. (Daughter Grace never reached adulthood)
2 CONT
2 CONT =Letters from the National Archives of Sweden=
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003897396773?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000190281317850 '''Register of Estates - Landsarkivet in Vadstena, Name Pig's head, Jöns, Noble Yes, Remark: Beata Gyllensvärd, 1646, 1674
2 CONC , File Göta Court of Appeal. The main archive (SE/VaLA/03825/01)''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000003897396773?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000191504729826 '''Letter to Per Abrahamsson Brahe. From women's hours, Sender, Beata Gyllenswärd, who is married to Jöns Svinhufvud''']
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://www.geni.com/photo/view?album_type=photos_of_me&id=6000000003897396773&photo_id=6000000201883271866&position=0 '''The National Archives' subject collections. Personal history of Jöns Carlsson Svinhufvud i Westergötland, 
2 CONC till Stora Dingelvik & Beata Persdotter Gyllensvärd SE/RA/756/756.1/S/S 100''']
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000002322154651?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000201884190843 '''The National Archives' subject collections. Personal history of Beata Persdotter Gyllensvärd, Year 1664 SE/RA/756/756.1/
2 CONC S/S 100''']
2 CONT
2 CONT *[https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000002322154651?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000201884238842 '''The National Archives' subject collections. Personal history of Beata Persdotter Gyllensvärd, Year 1686 SE/RA/756/756.1/
2 CONC S/S 100''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllensv%C3%A4rd_nr_240#TAB_44 The Noble Family Gyllenswaard No. 240]
2 CONT
2 CONT Father Per Joensson, Gyllensvärdleft, to Önnarp, and Hössna, both in Hössna, the county of Älvsborg. From Sunnerbo, in Småland. Adopted war service 1607, was a fighter at Västbo krektar 1618-03-26 and was 1622 at the Riga Lieutena
2 CONC nt in his brother-in-law Baltzar von Neuman's company of Swag Johan Hindersson Routers of Skälboö Regemente Västgöta Knektar (Skaraborg regemente). The captain of Nils Ribbing's West Govtegemente (Älvsborgs) 1624. Transfered to Vä
2 CONC stgöta rider 1628. Patterned as a rider at Smålands rider 1630-06-17 in Kalmar. Admitted 1632-08-12 in the field camp at Nuremberg, but the nobility letter first signed 1634-09-10 and confirmed 1647-04-20 (introd. 1638-01-17 under
2 CONC  number 240). Major 1632, at the end of the year. Lieutenant Colonel 1633 and then brought in nine with top tenants commanded over the regiment during the visit of Lützen, Fredrik Stenbock, at home in the country. Exit from the Re
2 CONC gistry in 1641, when he was not appointed to his Colonel. Head of a nobility company at the outbreak of the war with Denmark in 1644, contributing substantially to the successful outcome of the battle at Önsvalla Pass in Halland. 
2 CONC Dismissed 1656. Death 1664-03-19 and buried in the midsummer's day in Hössna church. He bought 1626 Önnarps tax yard, etc. in Hössna socken, and received 1629-03-03 peace of mind in a pleasant time. During the following three deca
2 CONC des he formed through the purchase of the tax and krono home in Västergötland and Småland the seas Önnarp and Hössna as well as Prästtorp in the Berga parish, Kronoberg County. [ 1 ]. Married to Elisabet Hand , to Hössna and Gavlö
2 CONC , born 1598, died 1651-04-10 and buried in Hössna church, daughter of the governor Håkan Hand , and Virginia, King Erik XIV's natural daughter with Agda Persdotter.
2 CONT
2 CONT =Children:=
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Johan,''', born 1617. Rider. Death 1688. Married Stierna
2 CONT * '''Knut Regimental Quartermaster. ''' Married Lillie af Aspenäs
2 CONT * '''Virginia,'''  lived widow. Married 1641 with the underlayman Johan Gustafsson , left Örnevinge in his 1st marriage, died in 1685.
2 CONT * '''Märta to Önnarp,''' which was reduced to 1689 from her, born 1620, died 1694-11-11 Önnarp Sweden.  Married to Captain Jonas Larsson Silfverswärd. 
2 CONT * '''Jonas Larsson Silfverswärd,''' dead 1656.
2 CONT * '''Beata,''' Lived widow in 1698. Married to the major Jöns Svinhufvud in Västergötland, no. 199, died in 1659.
2 CONT
2 CONT [https://www.adelsvapen.com/genealogi/Gyllensv%C3%A4rd_nr_240#TAB_44 '''Source''' The noble family Gyllenswaard No. 240] 
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://arkivkopia.se/bok/runeberg-ladal LIGNELL'S DESCRIPTION, OVER COUNTY DAL]
2 CONT
2 CONT 3) Egdes 1563 by Mrs. Karin pä Dingelvik: 1577 by Nils Månsson on Bro; 1619 by Mrs. Margreta to Bro: 1637 by Carl Svinhufvud at Dingelvik; 1664 it was Jons Pig Headfarmhouse: 1681 by Mrs. Beata Gyllenswaard, is then called Bågenho
2 CONC lm and is listed under the title old farmhouse. Made until 1790 by the contract priest, Doctor Anders Sörström in Hesselskog: 1795 by his widow in 1809 by Carl Fr. Owl; 1850 by Anders Olsson in Grättved. 
2 CONT
2 CONT '''Source''' LIGNELL'S DESCRIPTION, OVER COUNTY DAL 
2 CONT
2 CONT =History=
2 CONT
2 CONT Beata Persdotter Gyllensvard’s mother was Elisabet Hakandotter Hand and her parents were Håkan Knutsson Hand and Virginia Eriksdotter Vasa. Virginia was King Gustav Vasa's and Queen Catherine of Saxe-Lauenborgs  first granddaughte
2 CONC r, daughter of Erik XIV of Sweden and his mistress Agda persdotter. Agda was called “Caritas” for her beauty, which King Erik XIV was weak for beautiful women. Virginia was born at Kalmar Castle on 1 January 1559.  Virginia receiv
2 CONC ed two more full sisters in 1564. The Sisters were brought up initially by King Erik XIV's sister Cecilia, she took care of King Erik’s children alongside a girl, named Karin Månsdotter. Karin was as beautiful as Virginia’s mother
2 CONC  Agda, so King  Erik XIV was also taken by her beauty and dared to marry a commoner.( Imagine if Gustav Adolf the great dared to marry his childhood sweetheart Ebba Brahe. Karin then gave birth to 14 children of which half reached
2 CONC  adulthood).  
2 CONT
2 CONT King Erik XIV, wanted to marry Virginia off to the Russian Grand Duke Ivan IV Vasilyevich (Ivan the terrible). The marriage, however, never happen. Virginia was given on 7 May 1585 by John III, six farms in the West, plus on 14 Ap
2 CONC ril 1589 by Duke Charles five estates and homesteads in Vadsbro härad, Skaraborgs län. This was confirmed on June 8, 1626 in a confirmation to Virginia Eriksdotter frp, Gustav II Adolf in a letter from Queen Christina on April 22,
2 CONC  1635 to Sal. Aldewan, who gave both Alamiri's and Virginia's daughter's direct heirs in a confirmation 29 January 1650 af Queen Christina. After Beata Gyllensvärd married Jöns Svinhufvud  and moved to the farm Röksberg in Mulsery
2 CONC d parish. They also had Röksberg and several other farms in Angerdshestra, constituted a known Gyllensvärdsfäste. In Röksberg the couple's first three children were born. First came a daughter Elizabeth born in 1647, then after he
2 CONC r, a son Johan Magnus born on 11 April 1649, then it was time for Carl Bengtsson's grandmother Maria Catharina to see the light of day, who was born on 13 March 1650.  Lieutenant Jöns Svinhufvud by Queen Christina made a donation 
2 CONC in the neighbouring parish of Angerdshestra on some homestead for diligent and faithful armed service by Jöns and his wife Beata and the male heirs in perpetuity. Then, when Charles X Gustav started his Polish war, it was time aga
2 CONC in for Jöns to head out to war. Beata and her family came along, which was not unusual at the time.  It wasn’t a bed of roses to be kids in the aftermath of war, often there was no food and the journey went on such roads, as we to
2 CONC day call vångavägar. Diseases such as plague and other deadly diseases were commonplace, plus the children were beat with rice was prevalent.  After following her husband Jöns through war,  all difficulties permissions we find Bea
2 CONC ta on June of 1659 in Bromshög field camp on the island of Zealand Denmark, where days after her husband's death on June 17 gave birth to a daughter. "June 17" is apparent from the letter she sent to Per Brahe on 29 June,  where s
2 CONC he tells them her husband Jons has died and she has given birth to a small daughter and wishes Per to be her Godfather. I citeraren part of the letter: "Your high speed packet Grefl: Exelents joins iagh sorrow falsely perceive," o
2 CONC f the Pope then aldrahögste hafuer my Sahl: K: man Svinehufuedh jemmerfulla Jöns this world called hafuer on June 17, klåckan nästleden between 11 and 12 if the night, and his siääl guhd frigde tröste migh fattigh bedröfuade Enkia
2 CONC  småå quarlembnade medh ahro my children again, in synnerheet een small daughter as aldrahögste of the Pope then migh now my Sahl: K.husband's sudden death begåfuat huilken ähr hafuer iagh, in mind, now the next Söndagh that ahr o
2 CONC n July 3 to doop and Christendom förfogha. Also countries to Eder's höghe Grefl: ödmiuka: begiäran my Exl, Mirabel high speed packet Grefl: Exell: wanted to prove migh the höghgunstlighe affection, and be vitne to the small child'
2 CONC s doop and Christendom. " Beata concluded with: "Beata Gyldensuerdh a maximum of bedrö-fuad's widow" Even by a response letter from Per Brahe on June 30 it will produce, to Beata offered Per Brahe to be Godfather to the child. Let
2 CONC ter from Brahe is very difficult to read, but quoting it with parts of Jan's interpretation: Edel and wel. Wife "Us scar Eder skrfvelse af 29 junij deraf inhandigat we fixed and well underkstats made in the order with sorgh eder K
