2 CONT The farm's history can be followed from the 1500 century. Around 1610, Mrs. Karin gel Bay was the first farm owner and was the arch over the major and District Judge. Jons Svinhufvud inherited the farm and took it to it’s current 
2 CONC construction, the county farmhouse. The timber Castle was built probably around 1640 and served as the farmhouse on the estate for the past 200 years.  A new Manor House was built in 1846 and the old farm house, which became the w
2 CONC ing building was left standing as a residence until 1858, as the  gästrumsflygel and workshop areas. The ägodelning house standing as a free basis was demolished and rebuilt on the Enets land in Steneby in 1938. The house plans ou
2 CONC tlines typical buildings from 1600-century. A förstugeparti in the middle of the House share both the 16 planes in a representation page with two halls and two chambers or private offices, and a casual side with kitchen, domestikr
2 CONC um, night cottage and house. The House has several beautiful period architectural details, Turf roof rests on solid timber floor surfaces and furukavlar. The doors have pretty riveted Baroque fittings and stable ingenious locks. T
2 CONC he Hoop House is a unique furnishings and collections which illustrate the building's historical heritage and must be experienced on the spot.(the data) If the House is taken from Olle Enbågens essay). In 1667, Beata was strict be
2 CONC ing of Vasa blood but she also had a good heart,   she honored Mulseryd church with a chandelier made of brass, then in 1673, voluntarily added to its collection. She also donated to Anders Mårtensson half the farm Sundsbyn in Ste
2 CONC neby, for his lifetime service as her servant and fishermen. Beata died probably on the yard bågenholm during the  winter of 1701-1702 because on 3 February 1701 at Bågeholm they established a testamentsskrift between the Lieutena
2 CONC nt Jöns Johansson Svinehufvud (Beatas grandchildren) and his cousin the Virgin Mary Bullock, wherein the Lieutenant bequeathed half of his unencumbered sätsgård Bogeholm to her, "making himself a free disposition, with the assuran
2 CONC ce that neither he nor his heirs in their lifetime  would argue or dispute it. This testamentsskrift was on "persistent invitation" mounted in most protocols, upon 8-10 November 1703. My assessment is that Beata was buried alongsi
2 CONC de their Hall. next to Jöns in Mulseryd Cemetery. 
