1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Leonard Kagg's Diary - Kagg described the battle of Hummelshof in his diary;  "On the same day, which was July 18, Major General Schlippenbach had a sharp action with the Russians at Hummelshof, when ours was soon 
2 CONC completely defeated, except for those who managed to escape, ours consisted of 5,000 men and Czermettoff 70,000 Russians; killed on the spot were cornet Wulf of the Revalske adelbanan; of the Rigiske adelbanan colonel Brakel, lieu
2 CONC tenant colonel Glasenopp; of Abol. cavalry lieutenant [https://www.geni.com/people/Lt-H%C3%A5kan-Ekelund/6000000096393512998 Ekelund], Boning, cornet Demoin. Of the Karelian squadron dragoons; major Demolin. Of the Ostrobothnian i
2 CONC nfantry regiment lieutenant Tiesenhausen, Rigman, ensign Kling.  Of the De la Gardie regiment killed  captain lieutenant Riman, regimental quartermaster Wollfeldtt, lieutenant Nassacken, ensign Stahl , adjutant Luftus, also of the
2 CONC  same regiment ensign Hind.  (Kagg, Leonard (1912). Leonard Kaggs diary 1698-1722 p. 35)
2 CONT
