1 NOTE {geni:about_me} =Arvid Pik=
2 CONT
2 CONT * Son of Åke Pik and Kristina Giedda
2 CONT
2 CONT * Covered from 1362 to 1385 (Östenson 1973; SD hk no. 8176 and SD hk no. 12920 respectively)
2 CONT * In preserved documents, Arvid Pik is first mentioned on 24 September 1362, when he and Nils Krumme sealed a change of ownership.
2 CONT * The last time Arvid is mentioned in life is on 16 July 1385, when Arvid Pik and Nils Krumme's brother Bengt Krumme were appointed as appraiser at the purchase of the old Trollegodset Ed by Drott Bo Jonsson Grip in Voxtorp, Östbo
2 CONC  district.
2 CONT * In between, he and his kinsman Jöns Abjörnsson sealed several letters, often concerning transfers of property to the bailiff Peter Knoppe and apparently as guardian of his wife Ingeborg Bengtsdotter (Lindorms family).
2 CONT * Ingeborg was probably the daughter of Bengt Lindormsson in his marriage to Margareta Pedersdotter Dudde and in that case a cousin of both the squire Jöns Abjörnsson and the bailiff Peder Knoppe. As a young widow, Ingeborg had in
2 CONC  1365 transferred her properties to Ebbe Pik (64:1 Lindorm).
2 CONT
2 CONT * Arvid Pik had daughters Estrid and Märta.
2 CONT
2 CONT * 21 K. H. Karlsson, Genelogiska anteckningar, PHT 1909, and DS 1769.
2 CONT
2 CONT * Mr. Ebbe Piik was a man, rich in coins and land, and that in addition to Rossared and Särö, he owned some 20 named farms and villages in Halland, as well as estates in Östergötland and Westergötland and Piiksborg Castle by Lake 
2 CONC Bolmen in Sunnerbo, county of Småland. This castle was a property of the family whose name it bore. That it was owned by Ebbe Piik is evident from the fact that Abraham Brodersson, who married his widow, later came into possession
2 CONC  of it, and that after his estate, which had been withdrawn to the crown, was returned to the family, his son-in-law Thure Stensson (Bjelke) in 1419 and his son Sten Thuresson, after his father's death in 1426, owned the castle un
2 CONC til 1434, when it was destroyed by Engelbrekt. Mr. '''Arvid Piik''', probably Mr. Ebbe's brother, lived at the same time at nearby Bolmsjö.
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=+Arvid+Pik&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=1&postid=sdhk_9670&tab=post SDHK no: 9670]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1370 April 21, Place of issue: Bolmsö.'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Arvid Pik transfers all his properties in Brännarp (in Rävinge parish) and Steninge (in Steninge parish), including the lease fee called bolpenningar, which he inherited from his (half) brother Johan Pik, to the bearer of the lett
2 CONC er, well-to-do man Axel Ryning. [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/dokument/sdhk/9670.pdf '''The issuer seals.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Additional text On the back: B re f at Arnwid Pik scøtæ Axel Rẏni n g ha n s goods j Bre n nethorp oc Stenu n ge a‑ j Gellerydz sokn y Sy n n er bo ‑a . Literature and commentary Ang. (half) brothers Arvid and Joh
2 CONC an Pik and the dating place Bolmsö in the parish of the same name see C. Härenstam, Finnveden und medeltiden (1946), p. 51; see also KH Karlsson in PHT 1909, p. 17 f.
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=+Arvid+Pik&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=6&postid=sdhk_12486&tab=post SDHK no: 12486]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1383 September 29, Place of issue: Tynnelsö''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Arvid Pik and Erland Algotsson certify that Mr. Vämund and Unno in "Bergom" sent "20 MR less than two hundred" to Linköping's cathedral, for which sum he pledged his property. Arvid Pik, [https://sok.riksarkivet.se/bildvisning/R00
2 CONC 03523_00209#?c=&m=&s=&cv=208&xywh=-417%2C-206%2C5431%2C4108 '''Erland Algotsson seal.''']
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Post-medieval copies:  Lars Eriksson Sparre's copy book, hs B 15, fol. 215v, National Archives
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=+Arvid+Pik&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=7&postid=sdhk_20738&tab=post SDHK no: 20738]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1426 August 15, Place of issue: Hester''' 
2 CONT
2 CONT Märitta", Arvid Pik's daughter and Peter Håkansson's wife , sells to Torbjörn Kärling her property in "Firishulta kvarn".
2 CONT
2 CONT * [https://www.geni.com/photo/view/6000000007104317421?album_type=photos_of_me&photo_id=6000000212688456842 '''Sources:'''] Original:  Or. perg. RA 0101  images Post-medieval transcripts:  Hadorph: III E 80 mf. 146; Peringskiöld: 
2 CONC E 68 reg: no. 161 (Stenh), no. 150 (Wennæs)
2 CONT
2 CONT ==[https://sok.riksarkivet.se/?Sokord=+Arvid+Pik&EndastDigitaliserat=false&AvanceradSok=False&page=26&postid=sdhk_9398&tab=post SDHK no: 9398]
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Dating: 1369 January 25'''
2 CONT
2 CONT Lars Svensson pledges for 13 marks pure silver to Arvid Pik and Johan Lalleson two farms in Hässlås in Stafsinge parish, two farms in Näs in Drängsered parish, two farms in forest with a mill in Gällared parish and a mill in Vessi
2 CONC ge (church village in Vessige parish) with supplements. The issuer and Peter Knoppe, Mr Tyrgils i Långaryd and Bengt Krumme seal.
2 CONT
2 CONT * '''Sources:''' Original:  perg., Private archives: DRA,Photocopy:  DK (loose, Miscellaneous + Private sheet booklet), Printed (in excerpt) Rep. Dan. No. 286, DD III:8, No. 271, transl. to modern Danish: Danmarks Riges Breve III:
2 CONC 8, no. 271,Printed regest DS 7835, Literature and commentary Fritz, Year 1369 - what the parchment letters have to tell (Yearbook for the National Archives and National Archives 1993), pp. 13 ff.
2 CONT
